  "$comment": "Hand-labeled from the pinned sample source (scripts/samples.json), not from Concentrate output. nsidnev/fastapi-realworld-example-app. Routes: every `@router.<method>(..)` decorator under app/api/routes, one label per route, with the full path composed by hand through `router.include_router(.., prefix=..)` in app/api/routes/api.py and app/api/routes/articles/api.py and `application.include_router(api_router, prefix=settings.api_prefix)` in app/main.py (`api_prefix` is `/api`, assigned in app/core/settings/app.py); the line is the decorator's first line. Env (Phase 32): the pydantic v1 `BaseSettings` of app/core/settings (no env_prefix, so each field is the upper-cased variable) read where a function uses `settings.<field>` or `self.<field>` inside the settings class, and `BaseAppSettings().app_env` of get_app_settings. The fields `config()` fills from `environments[app_env]` in get_app_settings are chosen at run time and are not labelled. Data access is not labelled: the repositories use aiosql query files and pypika, which the scan does not read (docs/known-limitations.md). Calls (Phase 33): every call site in app/api/ and app/services/ whose callee name is a function, method or class written in the repository, listed with Python's own ast module and decided by reading the code, not from the tool's output. A method called on a repository is labeled with the class of the receiver's annotation (articles_repo: ArticlesRepository, repo: UsersRepository); a call of a class runs its __init__, and a class without one (the pydantic models, RWAPIKeyHeader) runs library code: target null; super().__call__ in RWAPIKeyHeader runs fastapi's APIKeyHeader (target null); user.check_password in routes/authentication.py runs UserInDB.check_password (the repository returns UserInDB). get_repository(...) and get_current_user_authorizer(...) inside Depends(...) are calls and are labeled. Library calls with a name that nothing in the repository defines are not listed.",
